course: dictionary
lesson: 7573
title: A word for a leader
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A president is a leader. In some countries the head of state is a president, not a king or queen, and the president is usually chosen by the people in an election. «In 2008 Barack Obama was elected the first Black president of the United States.» Elected means the people voted for him.
explain: The word president also has a second meaning. It can be the person in charge of a club, a company, a college or an organisation. Look at the clues around the word to choose the right meaning. Is it about a country, or about a group? Then swap in leader and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Context helps you read the word well. «George Washington led the American army to victory and became the first president in 1789.» Led and victory tell you he was a leader, and the sentence is about a country, so this is the first meaning.
fact: A president is the leader of a country that has no king or queen, or the person in charge of a club, company, college or organisation.
fact: The President of the United States and the President of Ireland are heads of state.
fact: The UK, Canada, Australia and New Zealand have a king or queen as head of state instead.
fact: To run for president means to try to be chosen as president in an election. A vice president is the person who works just below the president and helps them.
fact: «George Washington» became the first president in 1789 and stepped down after two terms, showing that a president should not rule for life like a king.
exercise: «In 2008 Barack Obama was elected the first Black president of the United States.» What does elected mean? | Born in a special house | Given a golden crown | *Chosen by people voting | Made to stop
exercise: A class council is choosing a president for the class. What is a president here? | A map of the country | A king who lives in a castle | A bell that rings for lunch | *The person in charge of the council
exercise: Which country has a king or queen as head of state instead of a president? | Mexico | The United States | Ireland | *New Zealand
test: «George Washington stepped down after two terms.» What does stepped down mean? | Was crowned king | Fell over | *Left the job | Climbed down the stairs
test: Why was it important that George Washington stepped down after two terms? | He was tired of the army | He had no more money | He won a prize | *It showed a president should not rule for life like a king
exam: What are the two meanings of president? | A type of coin | *A country's leader with no king or queen, or the person in charge of a club or organisation | A king's helper | A big hall for meetings
